line are shown above.\n\nAccording to the regression model, what is the residual for the highlighted datapoint?" :question/worked-solution "The residual equals the difference between the actual value of the dependent variable and the value estimated using the linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\text{Residual}=\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe highlighted datapoint has coordinates $(4,70).$ So, our actual value is $y=70.$\n\nOn the other hand, the point on the regression line that corresponds to $x=4$ has the $y$-coordinate $50.$ So, our estimated value of is $\\overset{^}{y}=50.$\n\n![](images/04/041f64255345edf7ac37bd61e0ab97a93cc2696f028a53ba0896e0659966c2d8.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, the residual is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Residual} & =\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated} \\\\  & =y-\\overset{^}{y} \\\\  & =70-50 \\\\  & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186543587 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176033 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e77a14c-9943-5494-ae89-a77c7a1888d0" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Residuals From a Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b317e2f-e6dd-53e0-9e49-ee9c188855d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.5\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542753} {:answer/id #uuid "49bc7362-977c-5232-be6c-b5cfdd1ef847" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542844} {:answer/id #uuid "5619b467-5b18-5824-9a47-f5bbd8a4a4a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542873} {:answer/id #uuid "612936c1-41a2-55be-bcc4-3b8cf0813d4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.5\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542902} {:answer/id #uuid "b26c54e1-c250-50fe-b5f2-37358d367201" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543105}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5619b467-5b18-5824-9a47-f5bbd8a4a4a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542873} :answer-field/id #uuid "6f4f4e5c-e51e-5cea-9a0b-324f1c69bce1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543361}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f1b17b2b-5f71-5d88-80f9-025ec7f6d205" :question/math-academy-id "q-134808" :question/problem "![](images/08/08ce939458d5c298805692df7d10bed2abdcf81ec874da3f61dbe15f59fc141a.png)\n\nA biologist records the heights $y$ (in meters) of several oak trees at certain times $x$ (in years) after they were planted. The scatter plot for the data and the corresponding linear regression line are shown above.  \n\nAccording to the regression model, what is the residual for the highlighted datapoint?" :question/worked-solution "The residual equals the difference between the actual value of the dependent variable and the value estimated using the linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\text{Residual}=\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe highlighted datapoint has coordinates $(6,6.5).$ So, our actual value is $y=6.5.$\n\nOn the other hand, the point on the regression line that corresponds to $x=6$ has the $y$-coordinate $5.5.$ So, our estimated value is $\\overset{^}{y}=5.5.$\n\n![](images/ee/eedd1cadb2ba49fb95f9e18f9bef365942e53521e6894a270c9a1e1474f3ed71.png)\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Residual} & =\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated} \\\\  & =y-\\overset{^}{y} \\\\  & =6.5-5.5 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residual is $1\\,\\text{m}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186543550 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176033 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e77a14c-9943-5494-ae89-a77c7a1888d0" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Residuals From a Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "111c354b-41eb-5072-82a1-a27b376ef779" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15\\,kg" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542679} {:answer/id #uuid "32b8dd5f-70e9-5121-9de5-389361fe1956" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-25\\,kg" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542777} {:answer/id #uuid "3eb6331c-9c5e-5112-8172-2d2c6ae715e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20\\,kg" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542810} {:answer/id #uuid "5ecc3dc4-f5bd-51df-a791-7eef362a46eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "50\\,kg" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542895} {:answer/id #uuid "6748c281-3aeb-5426-9750-d7329ae49821" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15\\,kg" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542918}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "32b8dd5f-70e9-5121-9de5-389361fe1956" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-25\\,kg" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542777} :answer-field/id #uuid "9ed40114-2ba1-5996-b505-11a621544fa9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543401}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b2848e9c-e485-5752-8daf-a5d57b496ccb" :question/math-academy-id "q-134812" :question/problem "![](images/24/243a4212d1128a79203493bf672ad1c956fe0f48aad6abbb910de2861d99669c.png)\n\nA dog food company records data on the number of dogs $(x)$ sheltered at some kennels across the country and the corresponding amount of dog food $y$ (in kilograms) consumed in a month. The scatter plot for the data and the corresponding linear regression line are shown above. \n\nAccording to the regression model, what is the residual for the highlighted data point?" :question/worked-solution "The residual equals the difference between the actual value of the dependent variable and the value estimated using the linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\text{Residual}=\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe highlighted datapoint has coordinates $(10,175).$ So, our actual value is $y=175.$\n\nOn the other hand, the point on the regression line that corresponds to $x=10$ has the $y$-coordinate $200.$ So, our estimated value is $\\overset{^}{y}=200.$\n\n![](images/2c/2cd59a9ae9c7ad474a9d5a308d4b8f3c9b96be70acdf1e3613dfc4757ff01766.png)\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Residual} & =\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated} \\\\  & =y-\\overset{^}{y} \\\\  & =175-200 \\\\  & =-25.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residual is $-25\\,kg.$"}]}
